# Real data only — no CRM pollution

This is a real marketing-department product. The model path is validated. Proof of progress is **real agent extractions visible in the CRM**, not fixtures.

## Hard bans

- Do NOT insert mock, fake, simulated, or placeholder leads into Postgres / CRM
- Do NOT use `*.example.com`, names like `Tool Test`, `Sim Lead`, `Real verify`, or `source=pytest` / fabricated sources
- Do NOT write test seed data into the shared `marketing_db` used by Docker `app`
- Do NOT treat in-memory fakes or simulated agent runs as proof that Discovery → CRM works

## What counts as proof

- Live search (e.g. DuckDuckGo) → real titles, URLs, snippets
- Real agent runs in `agent_runs` / `pipeline_runs`
- Real leads with production sources (e.g. `source=discovery`)
- Inspection via `/crm/ui/leads`, `/crm/ui/runs`, `/crm/leads`, `/crm/agent-runs`

## Tests & scripts

- If writes are required for automated tests, use a **separate test database** — never invent companies in the shared CRM DB
- Smoke/verification must run the **real pipeline** against live tools/models, or stay read-only
- Cleanup: delete only non-real rows (`example.com`, `source=pytest`, sim sources) — never wipe real discovery leads without asking

## Default stance

When asked to test or verify: show **real** Docker + model + CRM results. Fake CRM rows are a regression, not progress.

```text
❌ BAD: crm_write_tool(..., {"name": "Tool Test", "url": "https://tooltest.example.com", "source": "pytest"})
✅ GOOD: run Discovery → inspect leads created from live search hits in /crm/ui/leads
```
